    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a favorable afternoon slate, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries the highest efficiency score of the day at 73.66. Facing a soft matchup against Burrows (xERA 4.71), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a 17% boost in SP skill utilization and a massive 14% platoon advantage, firmly anchoring our middle infield. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (72.42) remains a high-upside play against Pfaadt; his score is buoyed by his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which maintains his viability as a core stolen base threat despite a minor park penalty. **Kyle Tucker** (67.05) and **Andy Pages** (62.29) also provide reliable production, with the latter drawing a prime opportunity against the left-handed Freeland to solidify the outfield.\n\nWhile our top-tier hitters hold strong, we are managing several tight margins at the bottom of the lineup. **Drake Baldwin** (59.21) and **Nasim Nunez** (58.63) both hover near the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, providing acceptable value despite the risks associated with facing Peralta. **Nasim Nunez** specifically illustrates our strategy of prioritizing sprint speed, as his score is elevated by a 3% switch-hitter premium that keeps him in the lineup despite the order-position penalty. The most difficult bench decision involved **Dominic Smith** (53.44); while he secured the final UTIL spot, he only narrowly beat out internal reserves like **Cole Carrigg** and **Wade Meckler**. The optimizer favored **Dominic Smith** due to the specific platoon matchup against Peralta, though we remain cautious given the potential for limited plate appearances if the game script shifts.\n\nWe enter the day with a clean bill of health among active starters, though the injury list remains a drag on our depth. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** still sidelined on the IL, we are forced to lean heavily on the remaining roster to preserve our games-played caps. **Gunnar Henderson** is unavailable due to an off-day, placing the onus on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.99) to provide run production in the heart of the order. We will monitor the weather reports for the Peralta start closely, as any wind shifts in that park could further suppress the ceilings of **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**, though we currently view the lineup as optimized for our specific 5x5 category needs.",
